The shopkeeper gives me another shirt.
He tells me, "Madam, this shirt is bigger than that one."
I take that shirt.
There is a small trial room in the shop.
I go inside and try on the new shirt.
I look in the mirror.
This shirt is much better than the first shirt.
Its shoulders are exactly right for me.
This shirt is bigger and more comfortable than the previous shirt.
I come out of the trial room.
I say to the shopkeeper, "Dada, this size is exactly right."
"I want this very shirt."
He smiles and takes my first shirt back.
He puts the new shirt in a bag.
I say to him, "Thank you for exchanging the shirt."
Now I have suitable clothes for the monsoon.
My new raincoat and this shirt are both absolutely nice.
I step out of the shop.
Now I am fully prepared for the changing season.
